    "searchText": "realtime and replay connect to proctor websocket events, authorize subscriptions, and recover from bounded replay gaps. realtime and replay proctor exposes one authenticated websocket endpoint at /api/v1/websocket . realtime delivery accelerates an interface; durable http resources remain the authority. browser connections use the interactive session cookie and must present the installation's exact allowed origin. native clients can use an allowed bearer credential and may omit origin. the connection handshake does not grant every subscription: each subscription action and resource is authorized separately. see connect websocket for the current handshake parameters and protocol schemas. resume after disconnect replay is bounded and node-local. retain the most recent sequence or replay cursor exactly as the protocol specifies, then offer it when reconnecting to the appropriate node. a successful replay fills only the available bounded gap. if the server reports that replay is unavailable or incomplete: 1. stop applying incremental events for the affected scope. 2. refetch the authoritative resource or collection over http. 3. replace local derived state with that snapshot. 4. establish a fresh realtime position and resume incremental processing. never treat a missing event as evidence that durable state did not change. cluster fan-out and websocket publication occur after the durable commit and are best-effort effects. protocol errors after upgrade, protocol errors use stable typed websocket envelopes rather than rfc 9457 problem details. handle an unknown event or error type defensively, preserve ordering within its documented scope, and reconnect with bounded backoff. avoid tight reconnect loops after authentication or authorization rejection."
